## Authentication

Vestiaire Collective has been perfecting the way customers buy and sell with confidence since 2009, combining unrivalled knowledge and expertise to advance its mission of being the world's most trusted resale platform. More than 150 quality control and authentication experts work internationally across digital and physical authentication, with authentication hubs in the US, UK, France, Hong Kong, and Singapore. Each expert has a speciality, from luxury brands and streetwear to watchmaking and gemology. The process runs through four layers:

1. Customer Profile Verification - Customer profiles are verified to create safe community spaces and help buyers and sellers transact with confidence.
2. Digital Verification - The team uses technical expertise, machine learning algorithms, authentication technology, and AI systems to help ensure accuracy. In 2024, roughly 10% of listed items were rejected during digital verification, including for poor image quality and item condition.
3. Physical Authentication - Items sent for physical authentication go through a rigorous methodology. Authenticators check product origin, alterations, modifications, materials, finishes, typography, stitching, serial numbers, engravings, dust bags, invoices, and other details. Authenticators are trained at Vestiaire Collective's in-house Anti-Counterfeiting Academy, created in 2017, with more than 60,000 hours of training.
4. Quality Control - The quality control team ensures that each item corresponds to its description and advertised condition.

Anti-counterfeiting commitments: Vestiaire Collective is a signatory of the Charter for Fighting Counterfeiting on the Internet (2012) and the Memorandum of Understanding on the sale of counterfeit goods on the internet, facilitated by the European Commission (2024). Collaborations with Burberry, Chloé, and others promote circularity and authenticity. All authentication services are performed independently by Vestiaire Collective.

